# Author CSS / JS Pipeline

## The one rule that matters most

**The engine does not decorate pages. Users place their own CSS.** Every
line of CSS a user sees on their published page must trace back to
something they wrote in `Block.customCss` or `Page.globalCss`. If you write
CSS that ships with the engine and affects how a block LOOKS on the page,
you are violating ADR-03. Stop and flag it instead.

The only engine-authored CSS allowed:
- Structural attributes with zero visual effect (`data-block-id`, dropzone
  markers)
- `styles.module.css` files, and ONLY for editor chrome (sidebars, panels,
  toolbars) — never anything that affects the page document's look

## Pipeline (never bypass this)

```
raw author CSS
  → cssParser        (reject invalid; reject @import, disallowed url(), data: non-image/font)
  → customCssComposer (per-block: scope to [data-block-id="..."]; global: unscoped)
  → injectStyles       (canvas iframe AND Open Page <head> — same output, same composer)
```

```
raw author JS
  → shape validation only (isolation is the actual control, not validation)
  → customJsComposer   (sandbox wrapping)
  → injectScripts       (canvas iframe or Open Page document — never editor parent)
```

Never raw-dump author CSS or JS into a `<style>`/`<script>` tag without
going through the composer. Never write a "quick" inline style injection
that skips `cssParser`/`customCssComposer` even temporarily.

## CSS composer rejection rules (cssParser)

Reject: `@import`, `url(http…)`/`url(https…)` unless on host allow-list,
`url(//…)` protocol-relative, `url(data:text/html…)` or
`url(data:application/javascript…)`, SVG-with-script data URIs, selectors
targeting `html`/`body`/`iframe`/`parent`/`:root` that look like an escape
attempt. Allow: `@media`, `url(data:image/...)` / `url(data:font/...)`
under a size cap.

## Precedence

`block.customCss` (most specific) → optional compiled style panel (if it
exists) → `Page.globalCss` (least specific, loaded first). Do not change
this order without an architecture amendment.

## Custom JS

- Runs only inside the canvas iframe or the Open Page document — never in
  the editor parent.
- Network access is default-deny (`connect-src` empty/`'none'`). Only
  enabled via explicit host `allowedConnectOrigins` allow-list, reflected
  into CSP. Never wildcard `*` in production config.
- Respect the `enabled` kill switch and `runAt: 'domReady' | 'afterHydration'`.
- Gated by host capability `allowCustomJs` (default should be treated as
  stricter/off for low-trust tenants — don't assume it's on).

## Server-side re-validation (§22.6)

Client-side composer output is UX only, not authority. Any `onSave` /
`onPublish` implementation you write on the host side must re-run the same
reject rules server-side. Never trust that the editor UI already validated
it.
